    "body": "I agree with Anne's read of the PSL page implicitly forcing a punycode conversion as part of the algorithm called from URL. That said, the page also confusingly says \"Note: the list uses Unicode, not Punycode forms, and is encoded using UTF-8.\" which can easily lead to confusion.\r\n\r\n@sleevi might know who we could ask to add something more explicit to the algorithm to make the punycodization of inputs (and therefore outputs) more clear.",
