    "body": "> why you filed this against Infra and not URL?\r\n\r\nI was confused by the [PSL](https://publicsuffix.org/learn/) mentioning \"[HTML 5](http://www.w3.org/TR/html5/) (document.domain) \".\r\n\r\n>  make the punycodization of inputs (and therefore outputs) more clear.\r\n\r\nBut then, if a *Public suffix* is formally defined as an ASCII, punycode string (consistent with the [example](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#example-host-psl)), the *Public Suffix String*, formally is not a list of public suffixes?",
